N lassopack.pkg
D  1 May 2026
U 40
d 'LASSOPACK': module for lasso, square-root lasso, elastic net, ridge, adaptive lasso estimation and cross-validation
d 
d  LASSOPACK is a suite of programs for penalized regression
d methods suitable for the high-dimensional setting where the
d number of predictors p may be large and possibly greater than the
d number of observations. LASSOPACK supports both lasso and
d logistic lasso regression. The package consists of six main
d programs: lasso2 implements lasso, square-root lasso, elastic
d net, ridge regression, adaptive lasso and post-estimation OLS.
d cvlasso supports K-fold cross-validation and rolling
d cross-validation for cross-section, panel and time-series data.
d rlasso implements theory-driven penalization for the lasso and
d square-root lasso for cross-section and panel data. lassologit,
d cvlassologit and rlassologit are the corresponding programs for
d logistic lasso regression. The lasso (Least Absolute Shrinkage
d and Selection Operator, Tibshirani 1996), the square-root-lasso
d (Belloni et al. 2011) and the adaptive lasso (Zou 2006) are
d regularization methods that use L1 norm penalization to achieve
d sparse solutions: of the full set of p predictors, typically most
d will have coefficients set to zero. Ridge regression (Hoerl &
d Kennard 1970) relies on L2 norm penalization; the elastic net
d (Zou & Hastie 2005) uses a mix of L1 and L2 penalization. lasso2
d implements all these estimators. rlasso uses the theory-driven
d penalization methodology of Belloni et al. (2012, 2013, 2014,
d 2016) for the lasso and square-root lasso. cvlasso implements
d K-fold cross-validation and h-step ahead rolling cross-validation
d (for time-series and panel data) to choose the penalization
d parameters for all the implemented estimators. lassologit,
d rlassologit and cvlassologit extend support to the case where the
d dependent variable is a binary response. In addition, rlasso
d implements the Chernozhukov et al. (2013) sup-score test of joint
d significance of the regressors that is suitable for the
d high-dimensional setting.
d 
d KW: lasso
d KW: elastic net
d KW: ridge regression
d KW: adaptive lasso
d KW: cross-validation
d KW: high-dimensional models
d KW: regularization
d KW: penalization
d KW: sparsity
d 
d Requires: Stata version 13.1
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20240918
d 
d Author: Achim Ahrens, Economic and Social Research Institute, Republic of Ireland
d Support: email achim.ahrens@@esri.ie
d 
d Author: Christian B. Hansen, University of Chicago
d Support: email Christian.Hansen@@chicagobooth.edu
d 
d Author: Mark E Schaffer, Heriot-Watt University
d Support: email m.e.schaffer@@hw.ac.uk
d 
f l\lassoutils.ado
f l\lasso2.ado
f l\lasso2_p.ado
f l\lasso2.sthlp
f c\cvlasso.ado
f c\cvlasso.sthlp
f c\cvlassologit.sthlp
f r\rlasso.ado
f c\cvlassologit.ado
f l\lassologit.ado
f r\rlassologit.ado
f l\lassologit_p.ado
f r\rlasso_p.ado
f r\rlasso.sthlp
f l\lassopack.sthlp
f l\lassologit.ihlp
f l\lassologit.sthlp
f r\rlassologit.sthlp
e
